From: Andy
Subject: [PATCH] sw: compile out XML writer call in release builds

writerfilter's string attribute helper is active outside DBG_UTIL even though
all callers use it only for debug logging and the writer is never initialized
in release builds. Guard the libxml2 calls so --as-needed can discard the
otherwise unused libxml2 dependency from libsw_writerfilterlo.so.

--- a/sw/source/writerfilter/dmapper/TagLogger.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/writerfilter/dmapper/TagLogger.cxx
@@ -150,5 +150,6 @@
     void TagLogger::attribute(const std::string & name, const std::string & value)
     {
+#ifdef DBG_UTIL
         if (!m_pWriter)
             return;
         xmlChar* xmlName = xmlCharStrdup( name.c_str() );
@@ -157,4 +158,8 @@
         xmlFree( xmlValue );
         xmlFree( xmlName );
+#else
+        (void)name;
+        (void)value;
+#endif
     }
